The '''''Blue Ace''''' was a custom-built state-of-the-art [[starship]] [[pilot]]ed by [[Torra Doza]] that suited to her personality and racing skills, during the [[time]] of the [[Cold War]]. It could hold an astromech droid and was able to change the power of its laserblasts. Doza used it in several races, missions and helped defend the ''[[Colossus]]'' several times. It was also present at the [[Battle of Exegol]] between the [[Resistance]] and the [[Sith Eternal]].<ref name="Databank" />

{{Ship-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Well, one thing we do know is that among the 14,000 ships that arrive with Lando Calrissian over Exegol in ''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker'' are the ''Fireball'', Jarek Yeager's racer, and Torra Doza's ship|Pablo Hidalgo on the ship's appearance in ''The Rise of Skywalker''|<ref name="Bucket List" />}}
The ''Blue Ace'' first appeared in "[[The Recruit]]," the first episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]''. The episode was directed by [[Steward Lee]] and [[Saul Ruiz]], written by [[Brandon Auman]],<ref name="The Recruit" /> and first aired on [[October 7]], [[2018]].<ref name="Resistance Trailer">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-resistance-trailer|text=''Star Wars Resistance'' Trailer Revealed}}</ref>

Torra's racer took the designs from the [[snowspeeder]] and early concept art by [[Ralph McQuarrie]].<ref name="SW-Designing Star Wars: Star Wars Resistance">{{SW|url=news/designing-star-wars-resistance|text=Designing ''Star Wars'': ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref>

The ''Blue Ace'' was among the many starships that made up the [[Citizens' Fleet]] during the Battle of Exegol in the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']]. A photo-realistic model of the ship was created for the film by [[Industrial Light & Magic]].<ref name="Bucket List" />

